targets.expr:
sum by (source, target) (
  label_replace(
    label_replace(
      sum by (client, server) (
        rate(traces_service_graph_request_total{client!="", server!=""}[$__rate_interval])
      ),
      "source", "$1", "client", "(.*)"
    ),
    "target", "$1", "server", "(.*)"
  )
)

panels.description:
The same edges through the instant + `organize` + `rowsToFields` chain, which produces one field per edge named `client-->server`. Three overrides prove the ids are real, and none of them is expressible on Route A:

- `grafana-->prometheus` is pinned to purple and drawn dashed;
- `prometheus-->prometheus` — the self-scrape — is given a wider line and its own curveness so it reads as a loop;
- `user-->grafana` carries a data link into Explore, scoped to that pair's traces.

An instant query means one row per mark, so every reducer returns the same number and **Calculation** stops mattering — the cost of the route. Note also that the panel's edge weight is `rate(...[$__range])`, the average over the whole window, rather than the last scrape.

